From eae2d557a81bc80a042abbb7f0db8ea845a16a21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 21:26:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fix(post): G43.4 posts write the joint angles of the tilt
 chain
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Fanuc and Doosan DNM posts wrote the stream's pose letters (axis =
Ry(B)·Rx(A)·Z) as the A and B words. On the tilt head the A rotary
carries the B rotary, so the machine reads those words as
Rx(A)·Ry(B)·Z: a different tool axis when A and B both turn.

A prelude function, chainAngles, now solves the joint angles for the
nest order of the machine file, and the machine check judges the same
angles through machine::tilt_chain::joint_angles. A chain whose nest is
unstated, a pair rotary stated along -X or -Y, and a C turn on an
A-outer chain are refused by name.

Fixes #4417

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
